    "created_at": "2021-03-02T09:01:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-02T09:01:12Z",
    "body": "Can't you just check `document.readyState` and/or wait for `DOMContentLoaded` since deferred scripts all run at [that time](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#stop-parsing)? I guess I'd like see the concrete use cases for this.\r\n\r\nAn event might be the right API. Or maybe we just need to expose a boolean indicating whether the script has already executed or not. If the use case involves doing something in the case the script hadn't run yet or never runs, it's not useful to have a load event since load event will never fire in that case so you'd have to check the above condition anyway.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
